A1. From what is made the oil which lubricates the machinery of Government? ~ BANANAS
A6. What are Chesterfields supposed to do? ~ SATISFY
A11. What animals closely resemble man? ~ APES
A13. What is the most important of the metallic elements? ~ IRON
A14. What comes after all the others? ~ LAST
A16. What is necessary to any sitting room? ~ SEATS
A19. What is the largest city of Seward Peninsula, Alaska? ~ NOME
A22. What is rarely found in a modern artist's studio? ~ ART
A23. What is the most unnecessary thing found on most any tourist's car? ~ PENNANT
A25. Name a Chinese racket. ~ WAR
A26. In what direction is Portland, Maine, from N. Y.? (init.). ~ NE
A27. What are soldiers most interested in? ~ EATS
A28. What should every little pedestrian learn to do? ~ LEAP
A30. Of what state is Des Moines the capital? (abbr.). ~ IA
A31. What does your baby think is the sweetest thing about you? ~ CANDY
A33. What noun means employment? ~ USE
A34. What do auto trucks carry? ~ LOADS
A36. What river in France is 175 miles long? ~ AISNE
A38. What argument used by the Romans did their enemies get the point of? ~ SPEAR
A40. What do most politicians do who have a seat in Congress? ~ SIT
A41. What is a native of a city called? (abbr.). ~ CIT
A43. Who has something to say one day a year—and nothing all the rest? ~ VOTER
A46. From what river in the lower world did souls drink before passing to Elysium? ~ LETHE
A49. What adverb means "at the place"? ~ WHERE
A51. What is an abbreviation for Ordinis Sancti Augustini? ~ OSA
A52. What does the tired business man do during office hours? ~ RESTS
A54. What little word often makes a fellow the "happiest man in the world"? ~ NO
A55. What is the Porto Rican word for "mutton fish"? (Our advice is that you do the Verticals.) ~ SAMA
A57. What is a French conjunction meaning "but"? ~ MAIS
A59. What is an English conjunction meaning "similarity, likeness"? ~ AS
A60. What is a devilish little fellow? ~ IMP
A62. What should Cupid do for domestic warfare? ~ MEDIATE
A64. What do gold-diggers dig for? ~ ORE
A65. What could Huckleberry Finn never become? ~ NEAT
A67. What is an obsolete spelling for "assize"? ~ ASISE
A68. What can three never be? ~ EVEN
A69. What is an action in law for damages for a wrong as distinguished from an action founded on contract? ~ TORT
A71. What is gold to a gold-digger? ~ LURE
A73. What was Galileo tried for? ~ HERESY
A74. What stood between Hannibal and Rome? ~ ROMANS

D2. What cartoonist originated the Tammany Tiger? ~ NAST
D3. What kind of people are quick to learn? ~ APT
D4. In what direction is New York from Washington, D. C.? (init.). ~ NE
D5. What is $100 in the bank? ~ ASSET
D7. Name a river in France. ~ AISNE
D8. What President is famous for the Panama Canal? (init.). ~ TR
D9. What was one of the ancient Greek races? (abbr.). ~ ION
D10. What is found in Alaska? ~ SNOW
D12. What is a breezy little instrument? ~ FAN
D14. What weapon is used for killing whales? ~ LANCE
D15. What is a name for a plane or open surface? ~ AREA
D17. What verb means "to follow as a consequence"? ~ ENSUE
D18. What is it husbands tell in the wee small hours? ~ TALES
D20. What is the chief subject of interest with any young man? ~ MAID
D21. What is a synonym for obliterate? ~ ERASE
D23. What is it the woman does? (If so, why is the man always broke?) ~ PAYS
D24. What is Jack and the Beanstalk? ~ TALE
D27. What class of people are not noted for their taking ways? ~ EDITORS
D29. What does many a girl do to a good egg? ~ POACHES
D32. What is an unsophisticated person? ~ NAIVE
D35. What is the first sign of the Zodiac? ~ ARIES
D37. What term placed before a married woman's maiden name indicates her parentage? ~ NEE
D39. What has a lot of crust? ~ PIE
D42. Name something that has its place in the sun. ~ AWNING
D44. What would any college boy prefer to make than 100% in his exams? ~ TEAM
D45. What is it that runs from place to place? ~ ROADS
D46. What are the priests of Lamaism called? ~ LAMAS
D47. What adjective did Chaucer use to indicate—tried; superior? ~ TRIE
D48. What does the girl friend give before she gets the ring? ~ ASSENT
D50. Where do good ball players go? ~ HOME
D53. What weed is mentioned in Biblical stories? ~ TARE
D56. What food is preferred by Eskimos (plu.). ~ MEATS
D58. What Greek combining form indicates imperfection. (We'll help you out—the third letter is E—— Now you had better do the Horizontals.) ~ ATELO
D61. What is always on top? ~ PATE
D63. What is a short abbreviation of Independent Indian Investigators? ~ III
D64. Where is many a ham roasted? ~ OVEN
D66. What is a lofty rock—or high hill called in Devonshire, England? ~ TOR
D68. What word indicates a long, long time? ~ ERA
D70. What is the second note in the musical scale? ~ RE
D72. What letters in what order indicate that the young boy is well pleased with what he is eating? ~ UM


